vim-surround
============

. repeats ds, cs and yss (vim-repeat is installed).

CHANGE AND DELETE
  cs"'                            "Hello world!" becomes 'Hello world!'
  cs'<q>                          'Hello world!' becomes <q>Hello world!</q>
  cst"                            <q>Hello world!</q> becomes "Hello world!"
  ds"                             "Hello world!" becomes Hello world!
  ds{ds)                          ({ Hello } world!) becomes Hello world!

ADD
  ysiw]                           On "Hello", Hello world! becomes [Hello] world! (iw is a
                                  text object)
  cs]{                            [Hello] world! becomes { Hello } world! (use } for no
                                  space)
  yssb or yss)                    Wrap the line in parentheses: ({ Hello } world!)
  ysiw<em>                        Hello world! becomes <em>Hello</em> world!

VISUAL MODE
  V then S<p class="important">   Wrap the selected lines:

  <p class="important">
    <em>Hello</em> world!
  </p>
